```csharp
public void Update(GameState state)
{
    if (!IsEnabled) return;  // DefaultEcs gate

    foreach (var dialogEntity in _dialogs.GetEntities())
    {
        var dialog = dialogEntity.Get<DialogComponent>();
        var show = dialog.IsOpen;

        foreach (var e in dialog.Content)
        {
            if (!e.IsAlive) continue;

            // Show/hide based on dialog.IsOpen (modal state)
            var hasVisible = e.Has<VisibleComponent>();
            if (show && !hasVisible) e.Set<VisibleComponent>();
            else if (!show && hasVisible) e.Remove<VisibleComponent>();

            // Gate focusable controls based on modal state
            if (e.Has<FocusableComponent>())
                e.Get<FocusableComponent>().Disabled = !show;
        }
    }
}
```

**Interpretation:** The UI DialogSystem gates both **visibility** (add/remove VisibleComponent) and **interactivity** (set Disabled flag on focusable controls) based on a component flag (dialog.IsOpen). Game code remains unaware; the system handles modal gatekeeping.

